	(text "Fires into the polymer split ring (the light guide). Three GPIO-driven FETs,\nhardware PWM, zero standby current (no LED driver IC)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 304 27 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "5969bd7e-2583-4f5b-9b10-23f5cc761ebd"))
	(text "R values: 4.3-4.8 mA at VSYS 3.45 V, ~6 mA at 3.7 V, ~8 mA at 4.2 V (APTF1616 Vf curves, p.3).\nGreen/blue have little headroom at 3.45 V - firmware scales PWM by battery voltage.\nC510-512 10 nF at the LED pins keep RF off the halo lines (the LED sits next to the\nantenna feed). R520-522 hold the gateslow while the nRF's pins float during\nreset, so the halo never flickers at boot." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 304 112 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "5103788b-ef6c-4fc9-9ab4-4395515fe5c9"))
	(rectangle (start 15 138) (end 140 262) (stroke (width 0.254) (type dash) (color 72 72 72 1)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "9066c24c-1026-4fe4-bef9-e6dc645247c3"))
	(text "D · 16 Mbit SPI NOR — MX25R1635F (shared SPI with the display)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 16.5 139.5 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d37a3903-2ed2-4cfc-94e7-36dab72f10cd"))
